for the Supreme Court

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.492 align:start size:88% position:13%
over any kind of
ideological preference.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.263 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Do you think that
in normal times

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.465
and I don't even know how
to define that anymore

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:30.470
that because we'd be talking
more about ACBs qualifications

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:32.705
rather than the process

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.907
she strikes me as the
type of person that

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:36.809
maybe 30 years ago let's say,

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:40.179
she probably would have got 70
votes or something like that

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:41.881 align:start size:84% position:16%
do you think that
that's something like
that's fair to say?

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.983 align:start size:81% position:19%
- I think 98 votes
is fair to say.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.518
Scalia got 98 votes

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:48.955
and Scalia didn't try to
hide his views at all.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:51.791
Justice Ginsburg got
many, many, many votes

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.426
she didn't try to
hide her views.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:56.562
The tradition back
in the day was that

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:59.032
you affirm somebody
for the Supreme Court

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:00.333
if they're highly qualified,

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:02.368 align:start size:81% position:19%
that was broken
for the first time

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.604
with the Bork nomination.

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:06.673
Bork was extremely qualified,

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:07.874
he was a professor at Yale,

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:09.375
he was Solicitor General,

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:12.078
he was a judge, but he had
extreme right-wing views

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:14.580 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he didn't present
them effectively.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.050
He made statements in
front of the Senate,

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.484
which really put a
lot of people off,

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:20.353
including a lot of Republicans.

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:25.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so he failed the
confirmation process test

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:28.027
but it turned into
more of a principle.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:31.197
Look, when you get a
court, a Supreme Court

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:33.866
that doesn't affect the
lives of ordinary people

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:35.101
as the Supreme Court didn't

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:37.136
for the first hundred
years of its existence,

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:39.405
