00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:53.119 align:start size:97% position:3%
Why don't we get input into
who is put on the court

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:55.355
they're affecting
our daily lives?

00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:56.856 align:start size:84% position:16%
So, you know, there's
no free lunch.

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:59.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
If want the Supreme Court
to be de-politicized,

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.227 align:start size:84% position:16%
then the Supreme
Court should stay away

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:03.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
from making controversial
divisive decisions.

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:06.299
If they're going to make
controversial decisions

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:08.267
then they're going to
become politicized.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.336 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's what democracy
is all about.

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:13.473 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I'm guessing that
not much can shock you,

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:15.041
but is any of the language

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:17.510
coming out of the
Democrats right now

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:20.480
shocking to you in that
there's basically just a

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.582 align:start size:84% position:16%
let's burn it all down
feeling right now.

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:24.684
Not just let's pack the courts

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:27.186
but let's change the
electoral college.

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:30.256 align:start size:97% position:3%
Let's change every
institution that in many ways,

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:32.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone like you has
fought for your whole life

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:33.793
to strengthen?

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.328
- Yeah, because

00:06:35.328 --> 00:06:36.829
they're not interested in
changing the institutions

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.731
they're interested
in getting their way.

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:41.000 align:start size:84% position:16%
and whatever it takes
to get their way,

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.069
they're prepared to do.

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:45.304
If the shoe were on
the other foot again,

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:47.440
they would be the
strongest defenders

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.609
of these various institutions.

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:51.677 align:start size:88% position:13%
But they, you know,
there's an intolerance.

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:53.579
It reflects itself
on campuses today.

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:54.981
Why do we need free speech?

00:06:54.981 --> 00:06:56.482
We know the truth.

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:57.917
Why do we need due process?

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.652 align:start size:81% position:19%
We know if a woman
accuses a man,

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:01.788 align:start size:84% position:16%
of course the woman's
telling the truth

00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:03.656
and the man is guilty.

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:06.292
Why do we need any
of these processes?

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:08.261
We know, we know the truth.

00:07:08.261 --> 00:07:13.266 align:start position:0%
We're endowed with this special
ability to discern truth

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:14.934
and we don't need process,

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:15.868
we don't need speech.

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:17.370
We don't need due process.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.405
We don't need the Supreme Court.

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:20.940
We don't need the
electoral college.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.442
We don't need anything.

00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:25.545 align:start size:88% position:13%
Just give us the ability
to rule and dictate

00:07:25.545 --> 00:07:27.713
and we'll dictate
in the right way,

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:29.382
said Stalin and Mao,

00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:32.285
and many of the students
on college campuses today.

00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:35.121
- So I'm curious
with that in mind,

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:36.522
I've been making an argument

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.524
and I did not vote for
Trump four years ago,

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:39.759
I voted for Gary Johnson,

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:41.661
but I am going to vote
for Trump this time.

00:07:41.661 --> 00:07:43.663 align:start size:97% position:3%
I've been making an
argument that in an odd way,

00:07:43.663 --> 00:07:47.567 align:start size:97% position:3%
Trump is defending both
liberalism and conservatism

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:48.901
at this point in that

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.436 align:start size:97% position:3%
he's defending conservatism
that's obvious,

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:54.207 align:start size:97% position:3%
the judges and the policies
are fairly conservative

00:07:54.207 --> 00:07:55.775
and he's defending
liberalism because

00:07:55.775 --> 00:07:59.345
he's basically the last door,

00:07:59.345 --> 00:08:03.583
between the lefties just
ramming through everything.

00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:05.651
Does that make some
kind of sense to you?

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.453
As bizarre as it sounds,

00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:09.555
Trump is defending liberalism.

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:12.058
- Unintentionally, he's
defending liberalism

00:08:12.058 --> 00:08:14.260
and many conservatives
defend liberalism today

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.662
because it's their ox
that's getting gored

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:18.731
by the extreme left.

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:20.600
But remember I'm old
enough, you're not

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.869
to remember when it
was the conservatives

00:08:22.869 --> 00:08:25.071
who were suppressing
free speech on campus.

00:08:25.071 --> 00:08:27.006
I grew up during McCarthyism.

00:08:27.006 --> 00:08:28.841
And so, as you said
in the beginning,

00:08:28.841 --> 00:08:31.911
there's enough hypocrisy
to go around on both sides.

00:08:31.911 --> 00:08:36.148
What we need is a core
of liberal centrist,

00:08:36.148 --> 00:08:37.817
conservative centrists

00:08:37.817 --> 00:08:41.053
who have to work together
to preserve institutions

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:44.257 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
without regard to
what the outcome is.

00:08:44.257 --> 00:08:47.994 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
We have to be focused
on process and fairness.

00:08:47.994 --> 00:08:50.096 align:start size:88% position:13%
It was Felix Frankfurter
the great justice

00:08:50.096 --> 00:08:52.365
who said the history
of liberty is primarily

00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:54.734 align:start size:84% position:16%
the history of
process and procedure.

00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:55.968
If you get that right,

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:57.837
you're going to lose
the outcome sometimes,

00:08:57.837 --> 00:08:59.438
but next time you'll win.

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:01.374
But if you change the process

00:09:01.374 --> 00:09:04.010 align:start size:88% position:13%
and eliminate due
process and free speech,

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:05.177
democracy is done.

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:08.714
- Do you think there's
enough of those liberals

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:10.049
of those centrists?

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:11.684
Are there any left?

00:09:11.684 --> 00:09:13.152
I mean we can joke
about, you know,

00:09:13.152 --> 00:09:14.353
there being about 10 of us,

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:16.155
obviously there are
other, you know,

00:09:16.155 --> 00:09:17.557
just good folks out there,

00:09:17.557 --> 00:09:19.492 align:start size:88% position:13%
but it seems like
they've lost all power.

00:09:19.492 --> 00:09:21.861
I don't see any of
them represented

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:23.362
by the Democrats at the moment.

00:09:23.362 --> 00:09:24.330
I mean, where are they?

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.498
- Well, I think you're right.

00:09:25.498 --> 00:09:27.833 align:start size:84% position:16%
I would have thought
that Joe Biden

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:31.103
would be one of the
last of the liberals,

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:32.371
the centrist liberals.

00:09:32.371 --> 00:09:34.073
And I hope maybe he will be,

00:09:34.073 --> 00:09:36.709 align:start size:84% position:16%
but he has to
resist the pressure

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:40.212
from the squad and from the
people on the extreme left.

00:09:40.212 --> 00:09:41.480
Look we're going to see

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:44.550
a move toward court
packing immediately.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:47.520 align:start position:0%
And I know that Joe Biden
doesn't want to pack the court.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.622
And I know he won't
push court packing,

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:53.292 align:start size:97% position:3%
but what if the Senate and the
House passes court packing,

00:09:53.292 --> 00:09:55.061
will he veto it?

00:09:55.061 --> 00:09:56.596
Does he have the courage

00:09:56.596 --> 00:09:59.966
to stand up against his own
party radicals and veto it?

00:09:59.966 --> 00:10:02.134
And I think that's
the great question.

00:10:02.134 --> 00:10:03.102
And I agree with you.

00:10:03.102 --> 00:10:04.637
We need to build the center.

00:10:04.637 --> 00:10:06.072
We need to build,

00:10:06.072 --> 00:10:08.674 align:start position:0%
look, I used to have these
great debates with Bill Buckley.

00:10:08.674 --> 00:10:10.309
He was a centrist conservative,

00:10:10.309 --> 00:10:11.544
I'm a centrist liberal.

00:10:11.544 --> 00:10:14.380 align:start size:81% position:19%
You and I can have
these debates,

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.215
but I can't have any discussions

00:10:16.215 --> 00:10:17.917 align:start size:81% position:19%
